<node id="LLM">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">LLM refers to Large Language Models, a key technology in the study of natural language processing and generation.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="RAG">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">RAG stands for Retrieval-Augmented Generation, a technique that combines retrieval with generation to enhance the quality of generated text.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="natural language processing">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Natural language processing is a field of computer science, artificial intelligence, and linguistics concerned with the interactions between computers and human (natural) languages.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="natural language generation">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Natural language generation is the process of generating natural language from a machine. It is a subfield of natural language processing.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="computer science">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Computer science is the study of computers and computational systems. It encompasses both the theoretical and practical aspects of computing.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="artificial intelligence">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Artificial intelligence is the intelligence demonstrated by machines, in contrast to the natural intelligence displayed by humans and animals.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="linguistics">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Linguistics is the scientific study of language, and involves an analysis of language form, language meaning, and language in context.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="text processing">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Text processing is the manipulation of text by a computer, including tasks such as tokenization, parsing, and summarization.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="dialogue systems">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Dialogue systems are computer programs that interact with humans through natural language. They can be used for various applications such as chatbots and virtual assistants.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="chatbots">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Chatbots are computer programs that interact with users through a chat interface. They can be used for customer service, information retrieval, and entertainment.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="virtual assistants">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Virtual assistants are AI-powered software applications that can perform tasks and provide information based on user queries.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="computational linguistics">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Computational linguistics is the subfield of linguistics that uses computers to process and analyze language.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="data mining">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Data mining is the process of discovering patterns in large data sets involving methods at the intersection of computer science, statistics, and information theory.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="machine learning">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Machine learning is a field of artificial intelligence that gives computers the ability to learn without being explicitly programmed.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="neural networks">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Neural networks are a class of machine learning models inspired by the structure and function of the human brain.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="deep learning">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Deep learning is a subset of machine learning that structures algorithms in layers to create an "artificial neural network" that can learn and make intelligent decisions on its own.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="semantic analysis">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Semantic analysis is the study of meaning in language, including the interpretation of the text and the inference of the writer's intentions.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="sentiment analysis">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Sentiment analysis is the computational analysis of texts to determine whether the sentiment expressed is positive, negative, or neutral.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="text classification">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Text classification is the task of assigning a category to a text document, based on its content.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="information retrieval">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Information retrieval is the process of obtaining relevant information from large collections of data, such as databases.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="knowledge representation">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Knowledge representation is the field of artificial intelligence that deals with the encoding, storage, and use of knowledge.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="inference">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Inference is the process of drawing conclusions based on premises or evidence.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="reasoning">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Reasoning is the process of using logic to draw conclusions or make decisions.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="pattern recognition">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Pattern recognition is the process of recognizing patterns in data. It is a key component of machine learning and AI.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="feature extraction">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Feature extraction is the process of selecting a subset of relevant features from a larger set of features.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="vector space model">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Vector space model is a mathematical model for representing text data, typically as vectors in a high-dimensional space.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="term frequency-inverse document frequency">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Term frequency-inverse document frequency (TF-IDF) is a statistical measure used to evaluate how important a word is to a document in a collection or corpus.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="document similarity">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Document similarity is the measure of the degree to which two documents are alike.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="text clustering">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Text clustering is the task of grouping a set of documents into clusters based on their content.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="topic modeling">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Topic modeling is a statistical method for discovering abstract topics that occur in a collection of documents.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="document summarization">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Document summarization is the task of reducing a document to a shorter, more concise version while preserving the main content.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="question answering">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Question answering is the task of automatically answering a question posed by a user based on a collection of documents.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="factoid question answering">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Factoid question answering is the task of answering questions that have a factual answer, such as "Who was the president of the United States in 1990?".</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="open-domain question answering">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Open-domain question answering is the task of answering questions on any topic, not limited to a specific domain.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="cross-lingual question answering">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Cross-lingual question answering is the task of answering questions in one language based on documents in another language.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="zero-shot learning">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Zero-shot learning is the task of learning to classify examples of unseen classes without any training data for those classes.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="few-shot learning">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Few-shot learning is the task of learning to classify examples of a new class with very few training examples for that class.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="active learning">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Active learning is a machine learning approach where the model is allowed to query the human annotator for additional examples.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="semi-supervised learning">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Semi-supervised learning is a machine learning approach where the model is trained on a combination of labeled and unlabeled data.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="unsupervised learning">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Unsupervised learning is a machine learning approach where the model is trained on unlabeled data.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="supervised learning">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Supervised learning is a machine learning approach where the model is trained on labeled data.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="transfer learning">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Transfer learning is a machine learning approach where a pre-trained model is fine-tuned on a new task.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="domain adaptation">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Domain adaptation is the task of adapting a model trained on one domain to perform well on a different domain.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="out-of-distribution detection">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Out-of-distribution detection is the task of identifying examples that do not come from the same distribution as the training data.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="robustness">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Robustness is the ability of a system to perform well under various conditions, including adversarial attacks.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="adversarial examples">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Adversarial examples are carefully crafted examples designed to fool a machine learning model.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="explanation">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Explanation is the process of providing a clear and understandable explanation of how a machine learning model makes decisions.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="interpretability">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Interpretability is the degree to which a machine learning model's decisions can be understood by humans.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="explainable AI">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Explainable AI (XAI) is a field of research that focuses on making machine learning models more interpretable.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="algorithmic bias">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Algorithmic bias refers to the unfair or discriminatory outcomes that can result from biases in machine learning algorithms.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="fairness">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Fairness is the concept of treating all individuals equally, regardless of their characteristics.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="equality">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Equality is the state of being equal, or of having the same rights, status, or opportunities.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="inclusion">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Inclusion is the act of including or involving others, especially in a positive or welcome way.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="diversity">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Diversity is the quality of having an unlimited variety.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="accessibility">
  <data key="d0">category</data>
  <data key="d1">Accessibility is the quality of being easy to reach or use.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8970bd8a17e748042cb5c08933e67b74</data>
</node>
<node id="案例研究法">
  <data key="d2">chunk-ac001068fc7df3b11881c74da0e84540</data>
  <data key="d1">案例研究法用于提供实证支持，以验证研究假设。</data>
  <data key="d0">UNKNOWN</data>
</node>
<node id="案例研究">
  <data key="d2">chunk-ac001068fc7df3b11881c74da0e84540</data>
